# Speckit Specify: Automatic File Manager
# Detailed specifications for implementation

## 1. Application Architecture

### 1.1 Component Structure
```
FileFlow Manager
├── Backend (Python)
│   ├── Core Engine (fileflow_core)
│   │   ├── rule_engine.py      # Rule processing logic
│   │   ├── file_scanner.py     # File discovery and indexing
│   │   ├── file_operations.py  # Move, delete, checksum operations
│   │   ├── duplicate_detector.py # SHA-256 based duplicate detection
│   │   └── date_organizer.py   # Date-based folder organization
│   ├── Configuration (fileflow_config)
│   │   ├── config_manager.py   # TOML config read/write
│   │   ├── rule_schema.py      # Rule validation and schema
│   │   └── defaults.py         # Default rules and presets
│   ├── Storage (fileflow_storage)
│   │   ├── database.py         # SQLite operations history
│   │   └── cache.py            # Checksum cache
│   ├── CLI (fileflow_cli)
│   │   └── commands.py         # Typer CLI commands
│   └── API (fileflow_api)
│       └── tauri_commands.py   # Tauri IPC endpoints
├── Frontend (Tauri + Svelte)
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── routes/
│   │   │   ├── Dashboard.svelte    # Tab 1: Triggers & status
│   │   │   ├── Rules.svelte        # Tab 2: Rule configuration
│   │   │   ├── LargeFiles.svelte   # Tab 3: Large file management
│   │   │   └── OldFiles.svelte     # Tab 4: Old file management
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   │   ├── RuleEditor.svelte   # Rule creation/edit component
│   │   │   ├── FileList.svelte     # File listing with actions
│   │   │   └── ProgressBar.svelte  # Operation progress
│   │   └── lib/
│   │       ├── api.ts              # Tauri command wrappers
│   │       └── types.ts            # TypeScript interfaces
│   └── src-tauri/
│       └── src/main.rs             # Tauri bridge to Python
└── Configuration
    ├── fileflow.toml               # User configuration file
    └── fileflow.db                 # SQLite operation history
```

### 1.2 Communication Flow
```
User Interaction → GUI (Svelte)
                    ↓ (Tauri IPC)
                  Rust Bridge
                    ↓ (subprocess/HTTP)
                  Python Backend
                    ↓
                  File System
```

## 2. Configuration Schema

### 2.1 Main Configuration File (fileflow.toml)

```toml
[general]
version = "1.0.0"
auto_run_enabled = false
auto_run_interval_minutes = 30
log_level = "INFO"
log_retention_days = 90
checksum_cache_enabled = true

[paths]
screenshot_source = "auto"  # "auto", "desktop", "downloads", or custom path
screenshot_destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/screenshots"
default_downloads = "${DOWNLOADS}"

[detection]
large_file_threshold_mb = 100
old_file_threshold_days = 90

[rules.screenshots]
enabled = true
name = "Screenshot Organization"
description = "Organize screenshots by date into Downloads/screenshots"
source_patterns = ["Screenshot*.png", "Screen Shot*.png"]
source_directories = ["${DESKTOP}", "${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/screenshots/{year}/{month}/{day}"
organize_by_date = true
file_types = [".png"]
priority = 1

[rules.documents]
enabled = false
name = "Document Organization"
description = "Organize documents into Downloads/documents"
source_patterns = ["*.pdf", "*.doc", "*.docx", "*.txt", "*.rtf"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/documents"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".pdf", ".doc", ".docx", ".txt", ".rtf"]
priority = 10

[rules.images]
enabled = false
name = "Image Organization"
description = "Organize images into Downloads/images"
source_patterns = ["*.jpg", "*.jpeg", "*.png", "*.gif", "*.webp", "*.heic"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/images"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png", ".gif", ".webp", ".heic"]
priority = 20
exclude_patterns = ["Screenshot*", "Screen Shot*"]

[rules.videos]
enabled = false
name = "Video Organization"
description = "Organize videos into Downloads/videos"
source_patterns = ["*.mp4", "*.mov", "*.avi", "*.mkv", "*.webm"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/videos"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".mp4", ".mov", ".avi", ".mkv", ".webm"]
priority = 20

[rules.archives]
enabled = false
name = "Archive Organization"
description = "Organize archives into Downloads/archives"
source_patterns = ["*.zip", "*.rar", "*.7z", "*.tar", "*.gz"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/archives"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".zip", ".rar", ".7z", ".tar", ".gz"]
priority = 20

[rules.3d_printing]
enabled = false
name = "3D Printing Files"
description = "Organize 3D printing files into Downloads/3d-printing"
source_patterns = ["*.stl", "*.obj", "*.gcode", "*.3mf", "*.amf"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/3d-printing"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".stl", ".obj", ".gcode", ".3mf", ".amf"]
priority = 15

[rules.code]
enabled = false
name = "Code Files"
description = "Organize code files into Downloads/code"
source_patterns = ["*.py", "*.js", "*.ts", "*.java", "*.cpp", "*.c", "*.h"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/code"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".py", ".js", ".ts", ".java", ".cpp", ".c", ".h"]
priority = 20

[rules.audio]
enabled = false
name = "Audio Organization"
description = "Organize audio files into Downloads/audio"
source_patterns = ["*.mp3", "*.wav", "*.flac", "*.m4a", "*.aac"]
source_directories = ["${DOWNLOADS}"]
destination = "${DOWNLOADS}/audio"
organize_by_date = false
file_types = [".mp3", ".wav", ".flac", ".m4a", ".aac"]
priority = 20

[duplicate_handling]
check_by_checksum = true
delete_duplicates_with_same_checksum = true
skip_duplicates_with_different_content = true
log_all_duplicates = true

[notifications]
show_completion_notification = true
show_error_notification = true
show_duplicate_found_notification = false
```

### 2.2 Environment Variables
- `${DESKTOP}` → `~/Desktop`
- `${DOWNLOADS}` → `~/Downloads`
- `${DOCUMENTS}` → `~/Documents`
- `${HOME}` → `~`

## 3. Data Models

### 3.1 Rule Definition
```python
@dataclass
class Rule:
    id: str                          # Unique identifier (e.g., "screenshots")
    enabled: bool                    # Is rule active?
    name: str                        # Display name
    description: str                 # User-facing description
    source_patterns: List[str]       # Glob patterns (e.g., "Screenshot*.png")
    source_directories: List[str]    # Where to scan
    destination: str                 # Target directory (supports templates)
    organize_by_date: bool           # Create date-based subdirectories?
    file_types: List[str]            # Extensions to match
    priority: int                    # Execution order (lower = first)
    exclude_patterns: List[str] = [] # Patterns to exclude
    min_size_kb: Optional[int] = None
    max_size_kb: Optional[int] = None
    min_age_days: Optional[int] = None
    max_age_days: Optional[int] = None
```

### 3.2 File Operation Record
```python
@dataclass
class FileOperation:
    id: str                      # UUID
    timestamp: datetime          # When operation occurred
    operation_type: str          # "move", "delete", "skip"
    source_path: str             # Original file path
    destination_path: str        # Target path (if moved)
    file_size: int               # Bytes
    checksum: str                # SHA-256 hash
    rule_id: str                 # Which rule triggered this
    dry_run: bool                # Was this a dry run?
    success: bool                # Did operation succeed?
    error_message: Optional[str] # Error if failed
    duplicate_of: Optional[str]  # If duplicate, original file ID
```

### 3.3 File Metadata
```python
@dataclass
class FileMetadata:
    path: str                    # Full file path
    filename: str                # File name with extension
    extension: str               # File extension
    size_bytes: int              # File size
    created_at: datetime         # Creation time
    modified_at: datetime        # Last modification time
    checksum: Optional[str]      # SHA-256 (lazy loaded)
    matched_rules: List[str]     # Rules that match this file
```

### 3.4 Scan Result
```python
@dataclass
class ScanResult:
    total_files: int             # Total files scanned
    matched_files: int           # Files matching rules
    large_files: List[FileMetadata]      # Files > threshold
    old_files: List[FileMetadata]        # Files older than threshold
    duplicates: List[Tuple[FileMetadata, FileMetadata]]  # Duplicate pairs
    operations: List[FileOperation]      # Planned operations
    estimated_space_freed_mb: float      # Space that will be freed
```

## 4. API Specifications

### 4.1 Tauri Commands (Python Backend → GUI)

#### Scan Operations
```python
@tauri_command
async def scan_files(dry_run: bool = True) -> ScanResult:
    """
    Scan all source directories according to active rules.
    Returns what would happen without executing (if dry_run=True).
    """
    pass

@tauri_command
async def execute_scan(operation_ids: List[str]) -> ExecutionResult:
    """
    Execute specific operations from a scan result.
    Must be called after scan_files() to actually move/delete files.
    """
    pass
```

#### Rule Management
```python
@tauri_command
async def get_rules() -> List[Rule]:
    """Get all configured rules."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def update_rule(rule_id: str, rule_data: dict) -> Rule:
    """Update an existing rule."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def create_rule(rule_data: dict) -> Rule:
    """Create a new rule."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def delete_rule(rule_id: str) -> bool:
    """Delete a rule."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def toggle_rule(rule_id: str, enabled: bool) -> bool:
    """Enable or disable a rule."""
    pass
```

#### Configuration
```python
@tauri_command
async def get_config() -> dict:
    """Get current configuration."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def update_config(config_data: dict) -> dict:
    """Update configuration."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def detect_screenshot_location() -> str:
    """Auto-detect where screenshots are saved on this system."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def export_config(file_path: str) -> bool:
    """Export configuration to a file."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def import_config(file_path: str) -> bool:
    """Import configuration from a file."""
    pass
```

#### File Management
```python
@tauri_command
async def get_large_files(threshold_mb: int = 100) -> List[FileMetadata]:
    """Get list of large files across monitored directories."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def get_old_files(threshold_days: int = 90) -> List[FileMetadata]:
    """Get list of old files across monitored directories."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def delete_files(file_paths: List[str]) -> DeleteResult:
    """Delete specified files (with confirmation)."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def get_operation_history(limit: int = 100) -> List[FileOperation]:
    """Get recent operation history from database."""
    pass
```

#### System
```python
@tauri_command
async def get_app_status() -> dict:
    """Get application status (version, db size, cache size, etc.)."""
    pass

@tauri_command
async def clear_cache() -> bool:
    """Clear checksum cache."""
    pass
```

### 4.2 CLI Commands

```bash
# Scan and show what would happen
fileflow scan --dry-run

# Execute scan and organize files
fileflow scan --execute

# Execute specific rule only
fileflow scan --rule screenshots --execute

# List all rules
fileflow rules list

# Enable/disable a rule
fileflow rules enable screenshots
fileflow rules disable documents

# Show large files
fileflow files large --threshold 100

# Show old files
fileflow files old --days 90

# Show operation history
fileflow history --limit 50

# Export configuration
fileflow config export ~/fileflow-backup.toml

# Import configuration
fileflow config import ~/fileflow-backup.toml

# Auto-detect screenshot location
fileflow detect screenshots

# Interactive mode for creating new rule
fileflow rules create --interactive

# Run as daemon (check every N minutes)
fileflow daemon --interval 30
```

